  "description": "DynaSand continuous up-flow sand filter (Type A custom unit, HH_DynaSand_v1).\nTertiary polishing of secondary effluent: up-flow filtration through a moving sand bed\nwith simultaneous airlift washing; wash water is a constant fraction (fWash) of influent\nand leaves as a reject side-stream carrying the captured solids.\nBuilt-in coagulant response: set Dose,alum (mg Al/L) or Dose,fe (mg Fe/L) > 0 to engage\nalum / ferric chloride assistance (pilot-tested: alum 8-14, ferric 14-16 mg/L).\nCalibrated to the Qaha\nWWTP pilot: El-Gendy et al. 2026, Sustainability 18(12):6058, doi:10.3390/su18126058.\nWASH ROUTING: Wash reject carries separated solids. Route it to an external reject outlet or a treatment path with net solids wasting. Returning all wash directly to this filter's inlet gives no net steady-state removal across the combined system.\nCOAGULANT DOSES are empirical capture modifiers: this unit does not calculate metal addition, hydroxide sludge generation or dosing-induced pH changes.",
